# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version if you're
#   using pyenv. See https://github.com/pyenv/pyenv/blob/master/COMMANDS.md#pyenv-version
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, if you're executing system tests against a specific version of a library, pipenv can be used.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   According to poetry's documentation, the lock file should be version controlled.
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   According to pdm documentation, association files are useful if shared
#   https://pdm.fming.dev/latest/usage/project/#run-your-project
.pdm-python.path
.pdm-build/

